{"kind":"finding","id":"F-map-render-005-01","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/MapRender/RenderCompositionManifestTests.cs","line":649,"method":"StableHash_IsDeterministicAndNonNegative","category":"T3","severity":"Low","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/MapRender/RenderCompositionManifest.cs:1624; change the FNV-1a offset basis or prime -> test stays GREEN today, red once a golden value is pinned","what_it_asserts":"Same-process determinism, distinctness on a one-char change, non-negativity, and StableHash(null)==StableHash(\"\").","why_weak":"The contract the XML doc states is stability ACROSS runtimes and builds (it is deliberately not string.GetHashCode) and the value is exported into the manifest as sigHash, which harness readers compare across runs. No property asserted here pins the algorithm, so any deterministic non-negative replacement silently changes every exported sigHash.","proposed_action":"Add one golden assertion, e.g. Assert.Equal(<precomputed FNV-1a value>, RenderCompositionManifest.StableHash(\"abc|def\")), so an algorithm change must be an explicit decision.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"F-map-render-005-02","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/Rendering/SmoothingPipelineTests.cs","line":780,"method":"PannotationsHeader_WritesCurrentAlgorithmStamp","category":"T3","severity":"Low","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/PannotationsSidecarBinary.cs:112; bump AlgorithmStampVersion from 1 to 2 -> test stays GREEN, which is exactly the forgotten-bump case its comment claims to catch","what_it_asserts":"That a freshly written .pann header round-trips PannotationsSidecarBinary.AlgorithmStampVersion through TryProbe.","why_weak":"Writer and expectation read the same constant, so the stated purpose (catching a forgotten bump) is unreachable; it only proves the writer does not hardcode a different literal. The comment is also stale: it says Phase 6 bumped 2 -> 3, while the constant at PannotationsSidecarBinary.cs:112 is 1.","proposed_action":"Either drop the forgotten-bump claim from the comment and keep it as a writer-wiring assertion, or pin the literal current stamp value so a bump is a deliberate two-sided edit. Fix the stale 2 -> 3 wording either way.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"coverage","sut":"SmoothingPipeline.ShouldFitSection","sut_file":"Source/Parsek/Rendering/SmoothingPipeline.cs","sut_line":667,"case_kind":"boundary","proposed_name":"FitAndStorePerSection_BelowMinSamples_SkipsWithoutWarn","sketch":"Build an ExoBallistic/Absolute section with MinSamplesPerSection-1 frames; assert no spline is stored, no Catmull-Rom-fit-failed Warn is logged, and GetSplineCountForRecording is 0.","guards":"The frames.Count < MinSamplesPerSection gate is currently untested (the test named for it uses exactly 4 frames plus a NaN); lowering or deleting the gate would push short sections into the fitter unnoticed.","risk":"playback"}
